Count the fields that newlines separate with a regex FS and RS="".
In paragraph mode newline separates fields in addition to FS. With a
regular expression FS, awk_split() did split the record at newlines but
counted only the fields that FS separated, so NF came out short and the
fields at the end of the record were lost: with FS = ", *", the record
"a, b\nc, d" had NF = 3 and fields a, b and c. Count a field at each
newline too.

---
 editors/awk.c |    5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/editors/awk.c
+++ b/editors/awk.c
@@ -2193,8 +2193,11 @@
 				n++; /* we saw yet another delimiter */
 			} else {
 				pmatch[0].rm_eo = l;
-				if (s[l])
+				if (s[l]) {
+					/* a newline delimiter (RS="") */
 					pmatch[0].rm_eo++;
+					n++;
+				}
 			}
 			s1 = mempcpy(s1, s, l);
 			*s1++ = '\0';
